@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] checks-notifications-are-explicit-and-local
Check failure notifications MUST require an explicit per-device pull request follow,
scoped to its server and Pully account. They MUST NOT implicitly follow Inbox rows,
repositories, or the shared GitHub account's personal notifications. Unfollowing MUST
stop alerts and remove that PR's notification. Source changes MUST invalidate in-flight
responses before they post or persist state (Tavi, 21 Oct 2026: add notifications for
failed PR runs; approved first implementation is explicitly followed PRs).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] checks-notifications-baseline-and-dedupe
The first successful complete current-head snapshot after following MUST silently
baseline existing failures. Identical failed check occurrences MUST NOT notify again,
including after process restart. A newly failed check or distinguishable rerun MAY
notify, with head, stable check ID and available start/completion evidence in its
identity. Partial, failed or unknown-head reads MUST NOT advance the baseline. Cancelled,
skipped, neutral, successful and unknown outcomes MUST NOT be called failures. Timed-out,
action-required and startup failures MUST retain their distinct meaning (Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 notification request and approved first implementation).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] checks-notifications-respect-controls-and-target
Check alerts MUST respect both the local category switch and Android's permission and
channel controls. Permission MUST be requested from a follow/enable action, never a new
startup prompt. Re-enabling MUST NOT replay a disabled period's old failures. A tap MUST
validate the original server/account source and open a verified check target on the
subscribed PR or that PR's Checks page. Notifications MUST NOT change GitHub read/watch
state. Background work MUST use bounded network-constrained checks and MUST NOT promise
realtime push delivery (Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 notification request).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] notifications-ai-outcomes-explicit-ownership
AI result alerts MUST concern only server-accepted task IDs explicitly requested or
followed on this device while enabled, persist source/account-scoped ownership, and
MUST NOT adopt server task-list history. Missing, network or interrupted states MUST NOT
become done or failed; cancelled tasks MUST settle silently (Tavi, 21 Oct 2026:
notification expansion and approved device-started task outcomes).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] notifications-ai-outcomes-no-replay
AI result notifications MUST default off. Enabling MUST NOT adopt existing work, and
observed OS/category denial or disabling MUST clear pending eligibility. A repeated
authoritative terminal snapshot MUST NOT duplicate an alert. An identity reset MUST
cancel category notices and reject late replies (Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 notification
expansion and approved device-started task outcomes).
